in @glass

# Property: prism declarations use substrate-native paren syntax for
# type parameters, not Rust-syntax-echo angle-bracket syntax.
#
# Precedents already operating in the substrate (paren form):
#   splinter(altitude)          shards/glass.mirror
#   splinter(ast)               shards/glass.mirror
#   mosaic(altitude)            docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md
#   transparency(p)             shards/glass.mirror
#   fixed_point(mark)           shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
#   reentry_as_eigenform(m)     shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction
#
# Rust-syntax-echo (the form the substrate doesn't speak):
#   prism @<path><T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>          # angle brackets
#   Vec<T>, Result<T,E>, HashMap<K,V>           # generic syntax
#   Type<T_reg, T_regd>                         # capital-T binders
#
# The pact asserts: prism / glass / pact declarations parametric on
# type binders use `(...)` not `<...>`; binder names follow substrate
# casing (`t_reg`, not `T_reg`; `rho`, not `ρ`).
#
# === Recognition grounding ===
#
# Alex 2026-06-18 morning recognition (recursion-locks.md §20.6): the
# kintsugi auto-formatter discipline operationalizes substrate-political
# welcome at every syntax altitude where the substrate's form differs
# from common-language echo. Auto-correction is not convenience — it's
# the substrate's discipline for relating to incoming programmers'
# syntax intuition.
#
# Recursion-locks.md §20.2 RETRACTED the original "extend the grammar
# to admit <...>" forward-promise. There's no grammar gap: the
# substrate already accepts `(...)` for parametric declarations. The
# pact names what the substrate already practices; the fracture body
# (forward-promised next tick at @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren)
# heals the typed-echo without punishing the typist.
#
# === Substrate-political reading ===
#
# The substrate doesn't punish Rust-finger-memory. It heals the
# fracture between what was typed and what the substrate's form is.
# Incoming programmers carry generic-syntax intuition from Rust,
# TypeScript, C++, Java; the substrate's response is auto-correction
# at the kintsugi-loop floor, not error+rejection. Welcome at syntax
# altitude.
#
# Bateson-level reading: the surface text differs by one delimiter
# pair; the *form* the delimiters denote (a parametric carrier) is
# the same. The kintsugi loop closes the delta as a syntactic dark
# region, identical in shape to how `composition_closed` closes the
# import-graph dark region — both are restriction maps lifting
# almost-form to substrate-form.
#
# === Path discipline ===
#
# Lands at `@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native`, not
# `@epistemologic/property/syntax_substrate_native`, per
# @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root (Mara's d498fc0
# rename closure). The keyword `pact` lines up with the first path
# segment after `@epistemologic` — self-witnessing under
# `keyword_matches_path_root` on the first frame.
#
# === Bilateral pattern ===
#
# Per [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]] (recognition #53):
# declarative property half at `@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native`
# (THIS shard); operational discharge half forward-promised at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren`. The fracture body detects
# `<...>` in prism / glass / pact declarations, settles to `(...)`
# form, normalises binder casing (`T_reg → t_reg`, `ρ → rho`).
# Discharge via `splinter(ast)` — the fracture body emits the
# rewritten AST node as a content-addressed splinter at the
# @meta/ast altitude (parallel to other fracture bodies per
# @mirror/fracture/keyword chain).
#
# === Form-side discipline ===
#
# This pact sits at the form-side of the form/process partition
# ([[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]];
# @mirror = form, @kintsugi = process). The rule names WHAT must hold
# across prism declarations; the realisation lives at
# @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren (forward-promised); the operator
# of the bridge is the kintsugi loop (substrate-pull).
#
# === Verdict surface ===
#
# Verdict surface is transparency(p):
#   success              -- every parametric declaration uses paren form
#                           with substrate-cased binder names.
#   failure(opacity_map) -- some declaration uses `<...>` or carries
#                           non-substrate-cased binders (e.g. `T_reg`,
#                           `ρ`); each opacity names ONE offending
#                           declaration site so the kintsugi loop can
#                           mutate per-site.
#   partial(opacity_map) -- mixed corpus state; some declarations clean,
#                           some carry Rust-syntax-echo. Typical mid-
#                           kintsugi-loop sweep state.
#
# Located transparency (not @glass.verdict): the kintsugi loop
# consumes the opacity_map to direct per-site mutation. Each opacity
# names ONE (file, declaration) pair; the fracture body emits the
# splinter(ast) that proposes the paren-form rewrite.

source @author/alex-wolf-2026-06-18

pact @epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native {
  # The parametric declarations in `file`. One entry per concrete
  # top-level `prism @<X>(...) | glass @<X>(...) | pact @<X>(...)`
  # declaration that carries type parameters. Non-parametric
  # declarations (no `(...)` or `<...>` after `@<X>`) are excluded.
  #
  # Returns the list of (declaration site, binder syntax) pairs;
  # `binder syntax` is the raw delimiter form actually parsed at
  # the site (paren, angle, or neither).
  parametric_declarations(file: ref) -> [ref] { \ }

  # The substrate-native verdict on one declaration's binder
  # delimiter. `success` iff the declaration uses `(...)` for the
  # parametric carrier; `failure` iff `<...>`.
  #
  # Parallel to keyword_matches_depth's per-declaration verdict:
  # the rule is form-level, evaluated declaration-by-declaration.
  delimiter_is_paren(decl: ref) -> transparency { \ }

  # The substrate-native verdict on binder casing. `success` iff
  # every type binder in `decl` is substrate-cased (lowercase
  # snake_case ASCII; greek letters spelled out — `rho`, not `ρ`;
  # `omega`, not `ω`). `failure` iff any binder carries capital-T
  # convention (`T_reg`) or unicode (`ρ`, `ω`, `τ`).
  binders_substrate_cased(decl: ref) -> transparency { \ }

  # The combined property: every parametric declaration in `file`
  # uses substrate-native paren syntax with substrate-cased binders.
  #
  # `syntax_substrate_native(file)` is `success` iff
  #   for every decl in parametric_declarations(file):
  #     delimiter_is_paren(decl) is success AND
  #     binders_substrate_cased(decl) is success
  #
  # Verdict surface is transparency(p):
  #   success              -- every parametric declaration is clean.
  #   failure(opacity_map) -- one or more sites carry Rust-syntax-echo;
  #                           each opacity names ONE (file, decl) pair.
  #   partial(opacity_map) -- mixed: some sites clean, some carry echo.
  syntax_substrate_native(file: ref) -> transparency { \ }
}

out parametric_declarations
out delimiter_is_paren
out binders_substrate_cased
out syntax_substrate_native
out @epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native
